WEBVTT

00:02.160 --> 00:04.610
G-Goshiki-san! Uh...

00:04.610 --> 00:05.660
Wait!

00:05.660 --> 00:08.980
For tonight, I want to savor 
this wonderful feeling!

00:09.370 --> 00:13.280
Please don't say anything. Good night!

00:28.210 --> 00:31.340
I couldn't do any work.

00:40.600 --> 00:41.810
Ichiro.

00:42.240 --> 00:44.020
How about the zoo today?

00:44.470 --> 00:45.490
Can we go?

00:47.500 --> 00:50.800
Yeah, let's go! I did promise you.

00:50.800 --> 00:53.410
Okay! Great!

00:55.540 --> 00:58.310
<i>I'll have a change of scenery,
 then get to work.</i>

01:01.650 --> 01:04.050
I can't wait to see the baby giraffe!

01:04.050 --> 01:05.280
You know, Fumio?

01:19.280 --> 01:21.190
M-Machi...

01:24.480 --> 01:27.550
It's fine. We'll go another time.

01:28.010 --> 01:31.070
You sure? We could at least go eat.

01:31.070 --> 01:33.850
No, I'll play with Fumio.

01:33.850 --> 01:35.900
You can feel free to work, Ichiro.

01:37.420 --> 01:40.600
W-Want to at least bake something 
together this afternoon?

01:40.600 --> 01:41.710
Sure.

01:53.660 --> 01:54.750
Okay.

01:55.590 --> 01:57.560
I'll hurry and finish up with work!

01:58.180 --> 01:59.770
Let's see...

02:00.340 --> 02:04.890
A scene where the heroine goes to 
rescue the kidnapped protagonist.

02:06.890 --> 02:09.900
Alice and the
 Knight of Thorns

02:07.380 --> 02:09.890
Reconsider upcoming developments?

02:10.160 --> 02:15.560
Yeah. Your art's been on fire 
lately with all the combat scenes,

02:15.560 --> 02:20.900
but a lot of people are musing that it'd be 
good to also focus on the primary love story.

02:21.410 --> 02:22.530
After all!

02:23.130 --> 02:24.910
Emotion is important!

02:25.220 --> 02:27.910
More and more emotion.

02:27.910 --> 02:32.840
I thought way too much 
about emotion yesterday.

02:37.920 --> 02:40.790
Almost to the point of emotional collapse.

02:42.930 --> 02:45.030
I'm in love with you.

02:45.810 --> 02:50.060
No, no, no! She got all 
carried away, not me!

02:51.040 --> 02:53.580
And nothing else has happened since.

02:53.580 --> 02:58.180
I know, maybe it's that instinct to 
bond with the first thing you see!

02:59.630 --> 03:00.580
Cheep!

03:04.510 --> 03:07.270
Stop getting carried away, Ichiro!

03:08.760 --> 03:10.210
I'm...

03:11.210 --> 03:13.960
Kuga-san, I'm in lo—

03:15.340 --> 03:17.960
F-Focus!

03:28.180 --> 03:35.480
Looks like it started before I knew it

03:36.230 --> 03:41.280
Thanks to you, I'm all smiles

03:43.200 --> 03:51.250
The usual townscape lends 
charm to the two of us

03:51.250 --> 03:56.750
Funny how it looks like a starry sky

04:00.510 --> 04:02.590
Suddenly buying flowers

04:02.590 --> 04:04.590
Standing around in the kitchen

04:04.590 --> 04:07.810
Sending a photo, because 
the setting sun is pretty

04:07.810 --> 04:12.350
Trying to spend as much 
time with you as I can

04:12.350 --> 04:15.350
This is all new for me

04:17.230 --> 04:22.900
I hope tomorrow is like today

04:23.240 --> 04:29.450
I've never felt this way before

04:29.450 --> 04:35.040
We'll go on a date this weekend if possible

04:35.710 --> 04:40.960
But it's fine if we stay home

04:42.210 --> 04:45.430
I can't wait to see you

04:48.010 --> 04:53.020
<b>Episode 4</b>

04:48.010 --> 04:53.020
<b>Weather Conditions</b>

04:48.010 --> 04:53.020
<b>with the Princess</b>

04:57.890 --> 05:03.410
I thought I could go to the library to 
look for materials, but it's raining.

05:04.430 --> 05:06.400
I want more assistant gigs,

05:06.400 --> 05:09.500
but if I'm going to work from here, 
that requires going digital.

05:14.080 --> 05:17.320
I might as well study up 
until I can get that tablet.

05:31.460 --> 05:35.050
I did it again without even thinking!

05:39.730 --> 05:43.070
It's... This is...

05:46.370 --> 05:47.890
<i>This is love!</i>

05:49.010 --> 05:50.070
Of course.

05:50.520 --> 05:58.090
That time I couldn't resist encouraging 
Kuga-san was because I was being drawn to him.

06:00.100 --> 06:01.330
A date?!

06:01.740 --> 06:05.350
That was a shopping and 
shrine date, wasn't it?!

06:08.760 --> 06:12.670
That stuff, too! I could 
have savored it more!

06:14.830 --> 06:18.520
Developing a relationship from 
friendship is lovely, too.

06:18.860 --> 06:21.900
I suppose you could say I'm your fan?

06:27.520 --> 06:30.590
How did I say those things 
with a straight face?

06:34.000 --> 06:38.470
<i>Then again, I already went 
and told him how I feel.</i>

06:38.910 --> 06:44.340
<i>So much for my beloved pattern of neither 
side knowing the other loves them,</i>

06:44.340 --> 06:46.970
<i>and building up a relationship 
over ten volumes.</i>

06:48.930 --> 06:51.380
<i>What am I supposed to do from here?!</i>

06:52.030 --> 06:55.300
<i>O god of shojo manga! Please save me!</i>

06:58.360 --> 06:59.800
<i>Besides...</i>

07:04.600 --> 07:08.380
<i>I've already stung Kuga-san.</i>

07:11.140 --> 07:13.620
<i>How am I supposed to act around him?</i>

07:27.130 --> 07:28.470
Good morning.

07:28.770 --> 07:30.760
G-G-Good morning.

07:31.080 --> 07:34.600
Those two don't seem too happy.

07:39.690 --> 07:42.730
Yeah, the rain kept us 
from going to the zoo.

07:43.000 --> 07:48.300
Machi in particular was going on 
about wanting to see a baby giraffe.

07:48.300 --> 07:51.490
That is unfortunate.

07:53.780 --> 08:00.490
Well, I canceled plans to go to the library
 due to the rain, and I have some time.

08:01.710 --> 08:04.810
I wonder if I should say something to them.

08:04.810 --> 08:08.000
You mean like... play with them?

08:08.350 --> 08:12.010
Yes, I'm hoping we could all enjoy that.

08:14.220 --> 08:17.070
Honestly, that'd be a big help.

08:17.580 --> 08:20.770
Oh, and I'll join in as soon as I can.

08:21.120 --> 08:22.510
I'm on it.

08:24.670 --> 08:29.380
May this day end up being a 
lovely day for all of us.

08:29.380 --> 08:30.100
Yeah.

08:30.890 --> 08:33.210
Okay, I'll leave them to you.

08:33.210 --> 08:34.030
Right.

08:41.200 --> 08:46.280
<i>I-Is it going to be like 
yesterday never happened?</i>

08:48.660 --> 08:51.530
<i>I ended up acting like 
nothing ever happened!</i>

08:51.840 --> 08:54.460
<i>It's... It's hard to look him in the eye!</i>

08:56.120 --> 09:00.550
No, I need to devote myself 
fully to those two right now.

09:04.320 --> 09:07.820
Good morning, Machi-san, Fumio-san.

09:08.110 --> 09:11.050
Oh, Goshiki-san. Good morning.

09:11.050 --> 09:12.330
Morning.

09:13.950 --> 09:14.810
What's that?

09:15.040 --> 09:16.200
These?

09:16.200 --> 09:17.840
"Machi-rot" cards.

09:17.840 --> 09:21.700
They're original fortune-telling 
cards Ichiro made for me way back.

09:21.700 --> 09:23.850
Wow, lovely!

09:23.850 --> 09:26.830
Machi-san, could you tell me my fortune?

09:27.800 --> 09:29.090
I guess.

09:30.290 --> 09:36.040
<i>Lose the combat scene and draw some solid 
interaction between Alice and Mimi.</i>

09:37.110 --> 09:40.090
<i>There, they ought to find 
this touching. I hope.</i>

09:40.540 --> 09:42.710
<i>Okay, that'll do for now.</i>

09:43.490 --> 09:45.640
Hey, I'm finally done!

09:50.530 --> 09:52.680
What's the matter?

09:53.500 --> 09:54.890
Kuga-san...

09:54.890 --> 09:59.640
Well, I tried to have 
her tell me my fortune...

10:02.030 --> 10:03.340
Pick a card.

10:03.560 --> 10:04.380
Okay.

10:07.970 --> 10:09.330
I choose this one.

10:18.800 --> 10:22.060
But I ruined a card.

10:24.870 --> 10:25.950
No, no!

10:26.350 --> 10:29.110
It was already worn out 
and held together with tape!

10:29.590 --> 10:32.980
That's why I told her she doesn't 
need to worry about it.

10:36.020 --> 10:40.270
Oh, the ones I made when 
you were in kindergarten.

10:41.290 --> 10:45.000
I'll remake them, then. I'm done with work.

10:46.430 --> 10:48.270
You don't have to.

10:49.820 --> 10:52.380
Would you rather they be more traditional?

10:52.740 --> 10:54.620
No, not really.

10:55.040 --> 10:57.010
I liked the ones you did.

10:58.050 --> 11:00.120
You really don't need to worry about it.

11:00.550 --> 11:03.970
If you were to redo them, I'd want 
to see the source materials.

11:03.970 --> 11:06.650
You know, something like 
my favorite fortune-teller's book.

11:08.520 --> 11:11.130
So, it can wait until the weather's nicer.

11:11.390 --> 11:14.400
Machi-san, who's your 
favorite fortune-teller?

11:15.730 --> 11:17.610
Fruit Migahara-sensei.

11:18.270 --> 11:21.670
Then I will go pick up a copy.

11:21.670 --> 11:25.070
Like I said, it doesn't have to be today.

11:25.070 --> 11:27.280
Plus it's raining heavily.

11:27.650 --> 11:30.710
I was originally planning to 
go to the library anyway.

11:30.710 --> 11:32.270
Pay it no mind.

11:33.600 --> 11:39.100
I'd rather see your new creation 
than wait for a sunny day.

11:42.370 --> 11:43.710
See you later!

11:46.310 --> 11:47.800
Wh-Why?

11:48.190 --> 11:49.890
Why'd she end up going?!

11:49.890 --> 11:51.810
I'm not sure, either.

11:51.810 --> 11:56.300
But she was saying she wanted to 
make the day lovely for you two.

11:56.950 --> 11:58.670
Goshiki-san!

11:58.670 --> 12:02.490
Fine, then! Might as well 
get out the drawing paper!

12:10.260 --> 12:12.580
<i>The library's beyond the station.</i>

12:12.580 --> 12:17.520
<i>I don't think she's lost, but maybe
 I should have gone with her.</i>

12:18.320 --> 12:21.330
Ichiro, go check on her if you're worried.

12:23.160 --> 12:26.100
Yeah, sorry. Look after Fumio.

12:26.100 --> 12:27.550
You got it!

12:39.010 --> 12:41.720
<i>I wonder if Goshiki-san and 
the book are all right.</i>

12:47.820 --> 12:51.070
Kuga-san? What made you 
come out in the rain?

12:51.070 --> 12:53.010
I could ask you the same thing.

12:53.010 --> 12:56.760
Are you okay? I bet you're totally soaked.

12:57.030 --> 12:59.150
No, the books are dry.

12:59.150 --> 13:05.000
I borrowed Migahara-sensei's new release, 
and several books with tarot designs.

13:05.260 --> 13:06.500
I'll carry them.

13:06.500 --> 13:07.870
Thank you.

13:08.800 --> 13:10.480
Were you able to borrow your own?

13:10.480 --> 13:11.090
Huh?

13:11.500 --> 13:15.030
I mean, you said you were 
originally going anyway.

13:15.420 --> 13:17.070
Wasn't there a book you wanted to borrow?

13:19.510 --> 13:21.630
I totally forgot.

13:21.630 --> 13:23.140
You forgot?

13:23.400 --> 13:27.570
Th-This kind of thing seldom... well...

13:27.570 --> 13:29.260
Goshiki-san?

13:29.260 --> 13:33.880
No, maybe I've always been 
an absentminded person.

13:36.660 --> 13:38.730
Did I say something amusing?

13:39.720 --> 13:42.190
It's just, the word "absentminded"...

13:44.180 --> 13:45.180
Sorry.

13:45.410 --> 13:48.130
I see. Absentminded, eh?

13:51.250 --> 13:52.340
Thank you.

13:53.250 --> 13:54.300
Shall we go?

13:54.300 --> 13:55.050
Yes.

14:02.690 --> 14:02.940
<b>Fruit Migahara's Tarot Divination</b>

14:03.190 --> 14:05.070
Hexagram spread

14:08.070 --> 14:10.420
Hey, can you draw this card?

14:10.420 --> 14:11.330
With a cat picture!

14:11.330 --> 14:12.610
You know it!

14:12.610 --> 14:15.510
The thing about your brother? He can draw!

14:15.510 --> 14:17.080
Yeah!

14:17.400 --> 14:19.140
He's manga man!

14:19.140 --> 14:20.120
Man.

14:26.920 --> 14:31.180
<i>But you know, I really do 
like this sort of thing.</i>

14:33.020 --> 14:36.550
If you watch too closely, I get nervous.

14:36.550 --> 14:38.230
What's the harm?

14:40.910 --> 14:44.100
I like watching you draw.

14:44.100 --> 14:45.230
I like.

14:45.230 --> 14:48.140
Your small characters are 
lovely too, Kuga-san.

14:49.060 --> 14:50.610
Thanks.

14:50.610 --> 14:53.260
I'd like it if you could 
draw the card borders.

14:53.260 --> 14:55.230
Yeah, draw them!

14:55.840 --> 14:57.750
A-All right.

14:58.120 --> 15:01.180
They're one of a kind. That's high pressure.

15:13.490 --> 15:14.590
Done.

15:16.520 --> 15:17.640
What do you think?

15:24.440 --> 15:26.200
Thank you.

15:28.020 --> 15:29.160
Look at you, all bashful.

15:29.560 --> 15:31.420
So, want your fortune told?

15:31.690 --> 15:33.150
You too, Goshiki-san.

15:33.150 --> 15:34.940
Huh? Where is she?

15:40.020 --> 15:42.910
Now that we've come this far,
 let's go all out.

15:46.320 --> 15:48.830
I'm borrowing some clothes racks.

15:53.210 --> 15:55.190
Just do this, and...

15:55.190 --> 15:58.050
That does set the stage!

15:58.050 --> 15:59.620
And also...

16:04.060 --> 16:06.210
There, how's that?

16:08.060 --> 16:09.960
I like it!

16:11.060 --> 16:13.530
I'd like to get it even more authentic.

16:13.530 --> 16:14.560
Definitely.

16:14.880 --> 16:16.390
<i>What're they doing?</i>

16:21.600 --> 16:24.350
That's cute! Like the real thing!

16:24.640 --> 16:27.220
Stop it! It's embarrassing!

16:27.480 --> 16:30.210
You could do this for 
real someday, Machi-san.

16:30.210 --> 16:33.540
No, fortune-telling's just a hobby!

16:33.540 --> 16:36.590
I'll have a steadier job when I grow up.

16:36.590 --> 16:40.460
Isn't a fortune-teller what 
you want to be, Machi?

16:40.840 --> 16:47.740
Well, I mean, you said you were going 
to be sure to send us to college.

16:47.740 --> 16:49.430
How'd you know...

16:49.430 --> 16:52.810
Well, that was assuming 
you say you want to go.

16:54.200 --> 16:56.860
You can choose anything, 
if it's what you really want to do.

16:57.270 --> 16:59.860
I'll always have your back.

17:04.060 --> 17:05.310
Thank you.

17:06.210 --> 17:11.620
Of course, you'd be naïve to think you 
don't need to study to become a fortune-teller.

17:11.620 --> 17:12.770
Right.

17:22.060 --> 17:25.230
Fumio! You want your fortune told?

17:26.140 --> 17:28.770
Come on up! I'll do it!

17:28.770 --> 17:30.000
Sit here.

17:31.250 --> 17:35.240
This is great! A planetarium, 
in place of a crystal ball!

17:35.240 --> 17:37.270
We brought it out of storage.

17:37.570 --> 17:40.600
Um, thank you. For everything.

17:40.600 --> 17:44.410
Sure. It's beautiful when 
an idea takes shape.

17:45.250 --> 17:48.430
I'm glad I left the island.

17:50.820 --> 17:53.780
Why don't you start by 
just drawing whatever?

17:54.980 --> 17:57.300
You want to make manga, right?

17:57.840 --> 18:01.790
I think it's fine if a princess 
becomes a manga artist.

18:03.760 --> 18:04.610
It is!

18:18.320 --> 18:20.820
Both of us this time

18:21.020 --> 18:23.820
<i>Yeah, I like it better this way.</i>

18:33.250 --> 18:36.260
Please leave these here until tomorrow. --Kuga

18:36.680 --> 18:38.480
There we go.

18:40.070 --> 18:43.420
The planetarium Dad bought way back.

18:59.000 --> 19:00.020
Kuga-san?

19:00.560 --> 19:02.720
G-Goshiki-san!

19:02.720 --> 19:04.770
If you're cleaning up, I'll help.

19:05.310 --> 19:09.350
No, I'll have Machi and Fumio 
pitch in with that tomorrow.

19:12.190 --> 19:15.050
Um, about yesterday...

19:15.510 --> 19:18.810
I'm in love with you.

19:19.500 --> 19:20.650
I...

19:20.650 --> 19:21.970
Wait a minute!

19:24.960 --> 19:27.340
Let's see, well...

19:28.170 --> 19:31.560
I've been thinking, I'd better 
do this the right way, too.

19:32.440 --> 19:35.100
I was happy for the sentiment.

19:36.770 --> 19:42.150
But right now, it's hard to see myself 
in a relationship or married.

19:43.490 --> 19:48.210
Machi and Fumio are my only family. 
I want to make them my priority.

19:48.820 --> 19:54.140
And I really don't like the thought of 
a union that's been decided for me.

19:54.940 --> 19:59.370
As planned, I'd still like to 
annul my engagement to you.

20:00.930 --> 20:06.720
Like you said before, I think that 
would be best for both of us.

20:10.340 --> 20:11.970
K-Kuga-san!

20:11.970 --> 20:13.920
That's enough already!

20:14.290 --> 20:15.340
No...

20:16.230 --> 20:20.610
I need to be honest with you, too.

20:20.900 --> 20:26.820
But if you reject me any further, 
it will have negative effects on you!

20:29.130 --> 20:34.620
I'm sure you can fool me, so that there'll 
be no retribution from the pact.

20:35.210 --> 20:40.170
I realize there are times when 
honesty isn't considered a virtue!

20:41.610 --> 20:47.630
Goshiki-san, I'm really not... 
not good at this kind of thing.

20:48.140 --> 20:51.920
The idea of "first love" 
at my age seems iffy,

20:51.920 --> 20:54.900
and I get a sense that I'm lacking 
when it comes to emotional content.

20:55.170 --> 20:58.160
My dream job isn't stable.

20:58.160 --> 21:02.470
And I don't want more responsibility 
or to be a burden on anyone!

21:02.470 --> 21:04.390
Kuga-san! Kuga-san!

21:04.390 --> 21:06.030
Don't keep going!

21:06.520 --> 21:09.160
But now I've fallen in love with you!

21:19.620 --> 21:22.800
Would you like to go out with me?

21:28.270 --> 21:33.010
B-By that, do you mean the two of us dating?

21:33.560 --> 21:35.430
Th-That's the one.

21:41.710 --> 21:43.100
Gladly!

21:43.580 --> 21:45.720
<i>It's like we're at a bar.</i>

21:46.460 --> 21:48.700
I just wanted you to know how I feel.

21:49.110 --> 21:53.360
We'll figure out the rest... as we go.

21:53.660 --> 21:54.920
As we go!

21:54.920 --> 21:55.990
The rest?

22:01.590 --> 22:04.140
Goshiki-san?! Are you all right?!

22:04.650 --> 22:09.510
M-My heart's so full it's about to stop.

22:09.510 --> 22:11.830
Don't let that happen!

22:16.060 --> 22:27.650
A long red thread stretching 
into the distance

22:27.650 --> 22:38.800
Meeting you, even if it meant having 
to cross hundreds of light-years

22:38.800 --> 22:45.480
Maybe I'll slowly get used to

22:45.480 --> 22:52.390
The two of us going out to have fun

22:52.390 --> 23:02.230
A tug on my arm, by the bond 
that was formed that day

23:02.230 --> 23:08.090
A little at a time, we've 
come closer together

23:08.090 --> 23:12.880
More smiles for us

23:12.880 --> 23:25.690
That place I first learned of, and 
the shops we'll visit again tomorrow

23:25.690 --> 23:31.650
They'll all be part of these lovely days

23:31.650 --> 23:38.490
Looking forward to it, good night

23:46.140 --> 23:47.980
<i>Next</i> time we'll make it to the zoo!

23:47.980 --> 23:49.790
Machi-chan, what's your favorite animal?

23:49.790 --> 23:50.330
The giraffe!

23:50.330 --> 23:51.350
And you, Fumio-kun?

23:51.350 --> 23:53.270
The panda. What's yours, Chibi-chan?

23:53.270 --> 23:54.450
Huh? Ichi...

23:54.700 --> 23:55.590
Ichi?

23:55.590 --> 23:57.260
Ichigo daifuku! (strawberry mochi)

23:56.120 --> 24:00.110
<b>Episode 5</b>

23:56.120 --> 24:00.110
<b><b>At the Zoo with the Princess</b></b>

23:57.260 --> 23:59.010
That's not an animal.
